1)Coding is the basic skill behind modern technology.
2)It is the foundation for creating mobile applications, websites, and software systems that people use every day

#Companies use coding in many ways to run their operations, improve products, and stay competitive. Coding helps businesses work faster, smarter, and more efficiently.

1. Building products and services
Companies use coding to create websites, mobile apps, and software products. For example, e-commerce companies build online shopping platforms, tech companies develop apps, and startups create digital tools to solve customer problems.

2. Automating business processes
Coding is used to automate repetitive tasks such as billing, payroll, inventory management, and report generation. Automation saves time, reduces human error, and lowers operational costs.

3. Managing data and databases
Companies store and manage large amounts of data using coded systems. Programming helps in organizing customer information, sales data, and performance metrics. Data analysis and dashboards help companies make better business decisions.

4. Improving customer experience
Coding powers customer support systems like chatbots, recommendation engines, and personalized user experiences. For example, streaming and shopping platforms suggest content or products based on user behavior.

5. Ensuring security
Companies use coding to protect data through encryption, authentication systems, and secure payment gateways. Cybersecurity tools are built using programming to prevent data breaches and fraud.

6. Supporting communication and collaboration
Internal tools such as email systems, project management software, and collaboration platforms are developed and maintained using code. These tools help employees work together effectively.

7. Innovation and competitive advantage
Coding allows companies to experiment with new technologies like artificial intelligence, machine learning, cloud computing, and automation. This helps businesses innovate faster and stay ahead of competitors.

In short, coding is essential for modern companies. It supports daily operations, enables innovation, improves efficiency, and helps businesses grow in a digital world.
